\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Qualitative comparison at $\times 4$ on texture-dense hard samples. The leftmost panel shows the ground-truth image with the (red) crop region; the remaining panels magnify that region for Bicubic, IMDN, SwinIR-light, SRFormer-light, CATANet, DPRNet (ours), and the ground truth. DPRNet restores repetitive building grids and high-contrast line art with sharper, less aliased structure, on par with the strongest competitors. This is a qualitative comparison; the crops are hard examples chosen by high-frequency content rather than by per-crop DPRNet advantage, and quantitative PSNR/SSIM are reported in the main table.}}{10}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
